{"source": "designer", "id": 60, "type": "plan", "message": "Wrote designs/wall_bracket.py: an L-shaped shelf bracket built from one XZ profile (inner_radius knee fillet and outer_radius heel fillet applied on the sketch) extruded along Y to `width`, with corner_radius plan fillets on the four free corners, a centreline triangular rib (gusset_thickness wide, gusset_reach of each free leg, ramp edges filleted with gusset_edge_radius before the union), two M4 counterbored shelf holes opening to the bed face at x=(thickness+shelf_depth)/2 and y=\u00b1shelf_hole_spacing/2, and two M4 counterbored teardrop wall holes from the room side at z=(thickness+wall_height)/2 and y=\u00b1wall_hole_spacing/2. All hardware sizes come from library.standard_parts via counterbored_hole; every cutter/boss is wrapped in feature(); PARAMS match the brief card exactly; no forbidden literals. section_plane returns Y=0 through the rib.\n\nVerification: the harness check command and magic-cad run_check were both permission-denied in this run mode, so gates were replayed in the build123d MCP session: default and all 24 single-param min/max corners plus all-min and all-max build one valid solid; validate() passes (watertight, manifold); a STEP export reimported reads bbox 80\u00d760\u00d780, two \u00d84.5 X-axis holes 40 apart and two \u00d84.5 Z-axis holes 40 apart; harness-style overhang shares stay under 8% (brief) and 5% (support risk) at the worst sampled corners, well under the 15% limit; the only flat ceilings are the two 8 mm counterbore bridges on the bed face. Hole-spacing params change only hole position (fingerprint second moments catch that); every other param changes volume."}
